    <!-- 08 Format Libraries -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="formats">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">08 &mdash; Format Libraries</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">The real edge: repeatable format libraries</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">High-volume UGC isn't random daily creativity</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Winning teams build libraries of hooks, formats, and angles</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Creators remix; brands measure which formats actually convert</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The teams that win at Tech UGC don't rely on inspiration. They maintain living libraries of hooks, formats, product angles, comment prompts, and editing structures &mdash; and creators remix these into dozens of variants per week.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Each variant is tracked back to its parent format, so the brand can see which hook families drive views, which angles drive installs or signups, and which editing patterns retain attention past the 3-second mark.</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong>Hook library</strong> &mdash; opening 1&ndash;2 second patterns proven to stop the scroll</li>
          <li><strong>Format library</strong> &mdash; repeatable structures (POV, screen-record demo, before/after, listicle)</li>
          <li><strong>Angle library</strong> &mdash; product use-cases mapped to audience pain points</li>
          <li><strong>Comment-prompt library</strong> &mdash; calls that drive replies, saves, and shares</li>
          <li><strong>Edit pattern library</strong> &mdash; pacing, captions, B-roll choices, sound usage</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 09 Metrics -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="metrics">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">09 &mdash; Metrics &amp; Benchmarks</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Views are not the only metric</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Views matter, but they're a starting point</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Saves, comments, and conversions tell the real story</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Track winning hook rate to learn what's actually working</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A Tech UGC program optimised purely for views will produce viral content that doesn't move the business. Mature operators track a small portfolio of signals at the same time.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
